      <div class="container install-wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Get started</p>
          <h2 id="install-title">One line. That's the whole setup.</h2>
          <p>
            Open a terminal in your project, paste the line, press enter. Muse finds the AI
            tools you already have and connects each one over MCP, profiled per task:
            Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Windsurf, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Hermes, OpenClaw and
            70+ more.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ol class="install-steps">
          <li class="reveal">
            <span class="is-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
            <h3>Paste one line</h3>
            <p>No install step, no config file, no account.</p>
            <pre class="term"><code>npx musememory connect</code></pre>
          </li>
          <li class="reveal" style="--reveal-delay:80ms">
            <span class="is-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
            <h3>Muse wires your tools</h3>
            <p>It detects what you have and connects each one with only the tools its task needs.</p>
            <pre class="term"><code>memory hooks install   # optional: hands-free recall</code></pre>
          </li>
          <li class="reveal" style="--reveal-delay:160ms">
